  "query_preview": "..\nKey Message 1...A brief period of dangerous heat today, with very \nwarm, but less humid conditions Wednesday.\n\nLarge dome of high pressure will continue to expand into the lower \nGreat Lakes region today, with 850mb temps rising into the the 22C-\n25C range (99th percentile for mid July). This will support highs \nreaching the mid to even upper 90s across the Lake Plains, Genesee \nValley and Finger Lakes, with upper 80s to lower 90s elsewhere.\nSee Climate section below for today's record high temperatures\nat Buffalo, Rochester, and Watertown. Combining this very hot \nairmass with a plume of higher moisture advecting into the \nregion with Tds reaching the low 70s across the lower elevations\nwill result in heat indices climbing into the lower 100s across\nthe lake plains, Genesee Valley, and Finger Lakes region, even \nas high as 105 degrees. Elsewhere, peak heat indices will reach \nthe mid to upper 90s. A Heat Advisory remains in effect today \nfor all of Western and North-Central NY from 11 AM to 8 PM.\n\nA fairly stout 30-40 knot LLJ will be located just 1-2 kft off the \ndeck this afternoon into this evening, allowing a good portion of \nthose stronger winds aloft to mix to the surface. When combined with \na tightening pressure gradient, expect to see frequent WSW to \nSW'erly gusts in the 25-35 mph range, with a few gusts to 40 mph not \nout of the question northeast of Lake Erie and east through \nnortheast of Lake Ontario. This will at least provide some natural \nrelief to the heat, especially across those areas downwind of the \nlakes. That said, with lake surface temperatures generally in the \nlow to mid 70s, it's cooling effects will be much less pronounced \nthan earlier in the season.\n\nVery warm and humid conditions will remain into at least Wednesday \nmorning, before an approaching mid level trough and surface cold \nfront drop south out of eastern Canada ushering in cooler and drier \nair from north to south from late morning through the afternoon. \nHigh temperatures will still range through the 80s by early \nWednesday afternoon, but dropping humidity levels will keep heat \nindices about the same, or possibly even a bit lower than the actual \nair temperature.",
